1
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:05,315
[Panting]

2
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:50,944
[Growls]

3
00:02:19,556 --> 00:02:22,058
- [Whimpers]
- Shush !

4
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:24,102
[Whimpers]

5
00:02:24,144 --> 00:02:26,896
[Fence Rattling]

6
00:02:30,025 --> 00:02:32,068
I'm stuck !

7
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:35,155
[Sighs]

8
00:02:35,196 --> 00:02:37,824
- [Grunting]
- [Muffled]

9
00:02:37,866 --> 00:02:40,952
[Barking]

10
00:02:41,036 --> 00:02:43,663
- Get back.
- [Barking]

11
00:02:43,747 --> 00:02:45,665
- [Straining]
- [Barking]

12
00:02:45,707 --> 00:02:49,252
- [Straining]
- [Barking]

13
00:02:49,336 --> 00:02:50,587
- [Barking]
- Hmm !

14
00:02:55,842 --> 00:02:58,595
[Barking Continues]

15
00:02:59,512 --> 00:03:03,433
- [Growling]
- [Gasps]

16
00:03:04,392 --> 00:03:06,728
- [Gasps]
- [Growling]

17
00:03:16,863 --> 00:03:17,947
- [Gasps]
- [Whimpers]

18
00:03:18,031 --> 00:03:19,699
- [Door Creaks]
- [Gasps]

19
00:03:28,041 --> 00:03:30,502
- Mr. Tweedy.
- Eh ?

20
00:03:30,543 --> 00:03:34,297
What is that chicken
doing outside the fence ?

21
00:03:34,339 --> 00:03:36,716
Oh ! [Chuckles]
I don't know, love. I--

22
00:03:36,758 --> 00:03:40,345
Just deal with it.
Now !

23
00:03:47,602 --> 00:03:52,857
I'll teach you to make
a fool out of me.

24
00:03:52,941 --> 00:03:54,526
[Groans]

25
00:03:56,069 --> 00:03:58,863
Now let that be a lesson
to the lot of ya !

26
00:03:58,947 --> 00:04:04,577
No chicken escapes
from Tweedy's farm !

27
00:04:28,601 --> 00:04:31,229
[Snoring]

28
00:05:09,976 --> 00:05:11,603
[Gasps]

29
00:05:18,693 --> 00:05:20,695
[Chattering]

30
00:05:32,665 --> 00:05:35,126
[Chattering]

31
00:05:42,175 --> 00:05:44,678
Oh !

32
00:05:46,262 --> 00:05:48,932
[Screams]

33
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:31,182
- [Gasps]
- [Growls]

34
00:06:53,663 --> 00:06:55,582
[Screaming]

35
00:07:09,929 --> 00:07:12,307
[Metallic Thumping]

36
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:15,143
- [Thumping Continues]
- [Sheep Baaing]

37
00:07:21,566 --> 00:07:25,111
Morning, Ginger.
Back from holiday ?

38
00:07:25,153 --> 00:07:27,113
I wasn't on holiday,
Babs.

39
00:07:27,155 --> 00:07:29,324
I was in
solitary confinement.

40
00:07:29,366 --> 00:07:32,369
Oh, it's nice to get a bit
of time to yourself, isn't it ?

41
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:35,789
[Bell Ringing]

42
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:39,793
[Clears Throat]
Roll call !

43
00:07:39,876 --> 00:07:41,836
Come along now.
You'll be late for parade.

44
00:07:41,878 --> 00:07:45,173
Pip, pip. Quick march.
Left, right, left, right.

45
00:07:45,256 --> 00:07:48,718
- Left, right, left, right !
Come on. Smarten up.
- Ooh !

46
00:07:48,802 --> 00:07:50,762
Discipline! Order!

47
00:07:50,845 --> 00:07:54,641
Back in my R.A.F. days when the
senior officer called for a scramble,

48
00:07:54,724 --> 00:07:57,227
you'd hop in the old crate
and tallyho.

49
00:07:57,310 --> 00:08:01,690
- Chocks away !
- Give over, you old fool.
They just want to count us.

50
00:08:01,773 --> 00:08:04,651
Oh, how dare you talk back
to a senior ranking officer.

51
00:08:04,734 --> 00:08:08,613
- Why, back in my R.A.F. days--
- Fowler, they're coming. Back in line.

52
00:08:08,697 --> 00:08:10,740
- Oh, right, right.
- Oh !

53
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:15,995
There will be a stern reprimand
for you, lad. You're grounded.

54
00:08:17,372 --> 00:08:19,541
Attention !

55
00:08:24,546 --> 00:08:28,675
Welcome back, hen.
Is there a new plan ?

56
00:08:39,144 --> 00:08:40,186
[Gulping]

57
00:08:44,232 --> 00:08:47,694
I thought we tried
goin' under.

58
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:50,363
Ah ! Over. Right.

59
00:09:01,583 --> 00:09:03,543
How's the egg count ?

60
00:09:03,585 --> 00:09:05,628
I've laid five eggs
this morning. Five !

61
00:09:05,712 --> 00:09:08,006
- Well-chuffed with that, I was--
- Shush !

62
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:20,518
Oh, no. Edwina.

63
00:09:21,978 --> 00:09:24,606
Bunty, why didn't you
give her some of yours ?

64
00:09:24,689 --> 00:09:28,735
I would have. She didn't tell me.
She didn't tell anyone.

65
00:09:28,818 --> 00:09:30,445
[Squawks]

66
00:09:34,949 --> 00:09:37,994
[Gate Creaks,
Closes]

67
00:09:38,078 --> 00:09:41,498
Oh, is Edwina
off on holiday ?

68
00:10:11,695 --> 00:10:15,699
- [Thud]
- [Gasps]

69
00:10:24,082 --> 00:10:27,961
[Geese Cackling]

70
00:10:38,888 --> 00:10:42,767
[Sighs]
We've got to get out of here.

71
00:10:42,851 --> 00:10:45,687
Ginger!
Are we still on ?

72
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:48,356
Oh, we're on, all right.

73
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:52,360
Spread the word, Mac.
Meeting tonight in hut 17.

74
00:11:13,214 --> 00:11:15,175
Oh !

75
00:11:19,763 --> 00:11:21,806
You called? Nick and--

76
00:11:21,890 --> 00:11:24,768
- Fetcher.
- At your service.

77
00:11:24,809 --> 00:11:28,813
[Dog Barking]

78
00:11:28,897 --> 00:11:30,940
Over here.

79
00:11:33,943 --> 00:11:35,904
We need some
more things.

80
00:11:35,945 --> 00:11:38,406
Right you are, miss.

81
00:11:38,490 --> 00:11:40,742
- How about this quality
handcrafted tea set ?
- Uh, no.

82
00:11:40,825 --> 00:11:42,744
- Or this lovely necklace and pendant ?
- It's love--

83
00:11:42,827 --> 00:11:47,165
Or this beautiful little number,
all the rage in the fashionable
chicken coops of Paris.

84
00:11:47,248 --> 00:11:49,334
Simply pop it on like so,

85
00:11:49,417 --> 00:11:51,628
and as the French hens say,
''Voila !''

86
00:11:51,711 --> 00:11:52,921
That's French.

87
00:11:53,004 --> 00:11:57,634
That's two hats in one, miss.
For parties, for weddings.

88
00:11:57,717 --> 00:12:01,805
Oh, but madame, this makes you
look like a vision, like a dream.

89
00:12:01,846 --> 00:12:04,849
- Like a duck.
- No, thank you.

90
00:12:04,933 --> 00:12:08,269
We're making this. We need these things.
Can you get them ?

91
00:12:08,353 --> 00:12:12,107
Oh, oh, oh,
this is a big job, miss.

92
00:12:12,190 --> 00:12:15,527
Oh, bigger than the others.
No, no. This is gonna cost.

93
00:12:15,610 --> 00:12:18,530
Same as always.
One bag of seed.

94
00:12:18,613 --> 00:12:21,282
- You call this pay ?
- It's chicken feed.

95
00:12:21,366 --> 00:12:23,243
- What else could we give you ?
- Eggs.

96
00:12:23,326 --> 00:12:25,245
- Eggs ?
- Eggs.

97
00:12:25,328 --> 00:12:29,290
- We can't give you our eggs.
They're too valuable.
- And so are we.

98
00:12:31,001 --> 00:12:32,919
After you, Fetcher.

99
00:12:34,254 --> 00:12:36,172
After I what ?

100
00:12:36,256 --> 00:12:38,425
- Move !
- Ooh !

101
00:12:38,508 --> 00:12:41,761
##[Woman Singing, Indistinct]

102
00:12:45,390 --> 00:12:48,101
Hmm.

103
00:12:48,184 --> 00:12:50,395
Twenty-two and nine.

104
00:12:50,478 --> 00:12:53,314
Fourteen shillings
and three pence.

105
00:12:53,398 --> 00:12:56,693
Seven and six pence times three.

106
00:12:56,776 --> 00:12:58,695
Two and nine.

107
00:12:58,778 --> 00:13:02,032
Four pence halfpenny.

108
00:13:02,115 --> 00:13:05,744
D-oh ! Stupid,
worthless creatures !

109
00:13:05,827 --> 00:13:11,541
I'm sick and tired of
making minuscule profits.

110
00:13:20,675 --> 00:13:23,219
Hmm.

111
00:13:28,725 --> 00:13:29,934
Hmm !

112
00:13:31,353 --> 00:13:33,605
Oh, yes.

113
00:13:33,646 --> 00:13:35,940
Those chickens
are up to something.

114
00:13:36,024 --> 00:13:38,818
Quiet.
I'm onto something.

115
00:13:38,902 --> 00:13:41,154
[Mr. Tweedy]
They're organized. I know it.

116
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:43,615
- I said, quiet.
- That ginger one.

117
00:13:43,656 --> 00:13:45,617
I reckon she's their leader.

118
00:13:45,700 --> 00:13:47,869
- Mr. Tweedy !
- [Gasps]

119
00:13:47,952 --> 00:13:51,664
I may finally have found a way
to make us some real money around here,

120
00:13:51,706 --> 00:13:53,667
and what are you on about ?

121
00:13:53,750 --> 00:13:55,669
Ridiculous notions
Of escaping chickens.

122
00:13:55,752 --> 00:14:00,757
- But-- But--
- It's all in your head,
Mr. Tweedy. Say it !

123
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:03,259
It's all in me head.
It's all in me head.

124
00:14:03,343 --> 00:14:06,596
Now, you keep telling
yourself that,

125
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:09,432
because I don't want to hear
another word about it.

126
00:14:09,516 --> 00:14:12,811
- Is that clear ?
- Yes, love.

127
00:14:12,894 --> 00:14:14,813
But you know that ginger one--

128
00:14:14,896 --> 00:14:17,732
They're chickens,
you dolt !

129
00:14:17,816 --> 00:14:21,486
Apart from you, they're the most
stupid creatures on this planet.

130
00:14:21,528 --> 00:14:26,866
They don't plot, they don't scheme,
and they are not organized !

131
00:14:26,950 --> 00:14:30,870
- [Chattering]
- Order ! Order !

132
00:14:30,954 --> 00:14:35,125
- Quiet, everyone. Settle down.
- [Chattering]

133
00:14:35,208 --> 00:14:40,046
I would like to call to order--
Please, if you could just settle--

134
00:14:40,130 --> 00:14:42,590
Let's have some discipline
in the ranks ! What, what!

135
00:14:42,674 --> 00:14:44,968
- Thank you, Fowler.
- In my R.A.F. days,

136
00:14:45,051 --> 00:14:47,929
we were never allowed to waste time
with unnecessary chitchat.

137
00:14:48,013 --> 00:14:50,181
Yes, thank you, Fowler.

138
00:14:50,265 --> 00:14:51,933
I--

139
00:14:54,310 --> 00:14:57,480
Right !
[Chuckles, Clears Throat]

140
00:14:59,357 --> 00:15:01,317
Carry on.

141
00:15:03,194 --> 00:15:07,365
Now, I know our last escape
attempt was a bit of a fiasco,

142
00:15:07,407 --> 00:15:10,452
but Mac and I have come up
with a brand-new plan.

143
00:15:10,535 --> 00:15:14,956
- Show 'em, Mac.
- Right. We tried going under
the wire and that didn't work.

144
00:15:15,040 --> 00:15:19,336
So, the plan is,
we go over it.

145
00:15:19,419 --> 00:15:22,130
- [Murmuring]
- This is us, right ?

146
00:15:22,213 --> 00:15:24,466
We get in like this.

147
00:15:24,507 --> 00:15:27,677
Wind her up
and... let her go !

148
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:32,766
[Gasping, Screaming]

149
00:15:32,849 --> 00:15:36,686
Good grief!
The turnip's bought it !

150
00:15:38,563 --> 00:15:42,192
Farmer's coming !

151
00:15:46,154 --> 00:15:48,448
Operation Cover-up !

152
00:15:50,450 --> 00:15:51,451
Whee !

153
00:15:52,994 --> 00:15:54,746
Ouch !

154
00:16:00,126 --> 00:16:02,170
Hmm.

155
00:16:06,591 --> 00:16:07,676
Huh ?

156
00:16:10,387 --> 00:16:14,724
[Clucking]

157
00:16:14,808 --> 00:16:18,520
- Mr. Tweedy !
- Ooh. Ouch.

158
00:16:18,561 --> 00:16:22,565
- Where are you ?
- Ooh. It's all in your head.

159
00:16:22,649 --> 00:16:24,818
It's all in your head.
It's all in your head.

160
00:16:28,154 --> 00:16:31,574
Think, everyone, think.
What haven't we tried yet ?

161
00:16:31,658 --> 00:16:33,576
Uh--

162
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:36,079
We haven't tried
not trying to escape.

163
00:16:36,162 --> 00:16:38,081
Hmm. That might work.

164
00:16:38,164 --> 00:16:40,792
What about Edwina ?

165
00:16:40,875 --> 00:16:44,713
How many more empty nests
will it take ?

166
00:16:44,796 --> 00:16:49,884
Perhaps it wouldn't be empty
if she'd spent more time layin'
and less time escapin'.

167
00:16:49,968 --> 00:16:51,928
So laying eggs
all your life...

168
00:16:52,012 --> 00:16:54,431
and then getting plucked, stuffed
and roasted is good enough for you ?

169
00:16:54,514 --> 00:16:56,766
It's a livin'.

170
00:16:56,808 --> 00:16:59,602
You know what the problem is ?

171
00:16:59,686 --> 00:17:04,274
The fences aren't just round the farm.
They're up here in your heads.

172
00:17:04,315 --> 00:17:08,528
There's a better place out there
somewhere beyond that hill,

173
00:17:08,570 --> 00:17:13,491
and it has wide open spaces
and lots of trees...

174
00:17:13,575 --> 00:17:15,535
and grass.

175
00:17:15,618 --> 00:17:20,331
Can you imagine that ?
Cool, green grass.

176
00:17:20,415 --> 00:17:23,835
- Who feeds us ?
- We feed ourselves.

177
00:17:23,918 --> 00:17:26,087
- Well, where 's the farm ?
- There is no farm.

178
00:17:26,171 --> 00:17:29,758
- Then where does the farmer live ?
- There is no farmer, Babs.

179
00:17:29,841 --> 00:17:33,970
- Is he on holiday ?
- He isn't anywhere. Don't you get it ?

180
00:17:34,054 --> 00:17:37,766
There's no morning head count, no
farmers, no dogs and coops and keys...

181
00:17:37,849 --> 00:17:40,894
and no fences.

182
00:17:40,935 --> 00:17:45,857
In all my life I've never
heard such a fantastic...

183
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:47,650
load of tripe !

184
00:17:49,194 --> 00:17:51,363
Oh, face the facts, ducks.

185
00:17:51,404 --> 00:17:54,949

The chances of us gettin' out of here
are a million to one.

186
00:17:56,034 --> 00:17:58,536
Then there's still a chance.

187
00:18:06,711 --> 00:18:09,297
[Groans]

188
00:18:20,392 --> 00:18:24,062
Oh, no, oh, no, oh, no.
What am I doing ?

189
00:18:24,104 --> 00:18:28,608
Who are you trying to fool ?
You can't lead this bunch of--

190
00:18:28,692 --> 00:18:32,862
[Grunts]
Oh, heaven help us.

191
00:18:34,948 --> 00:18:39,869
- [Explosion]
- [Screaming]

192
00:18:42,706 --> 00:18:45,834
Freedom !

193
00:18:45,917 --> 00:18:48,503
Huh ?

194
00:18:50,338 --> 00:18:52,007
[Chuckles]

195
00:18:55,218 --> 00:18:58,263
[Screaming]

196
00:18:58,346 --> 00:19:01,016
[Screaming]

197
00:19:02,475 --> 00:19:04,060

Whoa !

198
00:19:04,144 --> 00:19:07,522
Thank you, ladies and gentlemen.
You've been a wonderful audience.

199
00:19:08,898 --> 00:19:12,193
- Ouch !
- Oh, yes.

200
00:19:25,874 --> 00:19:27,876
- That's it.
- [Barking]

201
00:19:27,959 --> 00:19:30,295
Get him inside quickly.

202
00:19:30,378 --> 00:19:32,422
[Growling]

203
00:19:37,052 --> 00:19:39,471
This is our way out of here.

204
00:19:39,554 --> 00:19:41,348
We'll make posters ?

205
00:19:41,431 --> 00:19:46,644
No. What's on the poster, Babs.
What's on the poster. We'll fly out !

206
00:19:46,728 --> 00:19:50,774
He must be very important
to have his picture taken.
What do you suppose he does ?

207
00:19:50,857 --> 00:19:53,943
Isn't it obvious ?
He's a professional flying rooster.

208
00:19:54,027 --> 00:19:56,404
He flies from farm to farm,
giving demonstrations.

209
00:19:56,488 --> 00:19:59,157
- Do you suppose ?
- Oh, absolutely.

210
00:19:59,199 --> 00:20:01,493
Not in the dark, no.
No, not in there. No.

211
00:20:01,576 --> 00:20:04,162
Get out. Good.
Gotta get--

212
00:20:04,204 --> 00:20:06,831
[Muttering]

213
00:20:06,915 --> 00:20:09,000
[Groans]

214
00:20:09,084 --> 00:20:12,128
[Gasps] Who are you ?
Where am I ? What's goin' on ?

215
00:20:12,212 --> 00:20:14,631
Ouch ! What happened
to my wing ?

216
00:20:14,714 --> 00:20:16,633
You took a rather nasty fall.

217
00:20:16,716 --> 00:20:19,135
And sprained the anterior tendon
connecting your radius to your humerus.

218
00:20:19,219 --> 00:20:21,137
I gave it a wee bit of a tweak,
Jimmy, and wrapped her up.

219
00:20:21,221 --> 00:20:24,391
- Was that English ?
- She said you sprained your wing.
She fixed it.

220
00:20:24,474 --> 00:20:28,269
- I made the bandage.
- I-I carried you in.

221
00:20:28,353 --> 00:20:31,189
- [Chattering]
- Whoa. Whoa. Whoa ! Whoa.

222
00:20:31,272 --> 00:20:35,527
[Chuckles] Let's back up
and start from the top. Where am I ?

223
00:20:35,610 --> 00:20:38,571
You're right. How rude of us.
We're just very excit--

224
00:20:38,613 --> 00:20:40,573
This is a chicken farm.

225
00:20:40,657 --> 00:20:42,659
And we're the chickens.

226
00:20:42,742 --> 00:20:45,453
Yeah, with you so far.
Chicken farm, chickens--

227
00:20:45,537 --> 00:20:49,207
I don't like the look of this one.
His eyes are too close together.

228
00:20:49,290 --> 00:20:52,127
- Father, please.
- And he's a Yank !

229
00:20:52,168 --> 00:20:54,671
Easy, Pops. Cockfighting's
illegal where I come from.

230
00:20:54,754 --> 00:20:56,715
And where is that exactly ?

231
00:20:56,756 --> 00:20:59,759
Just a little place I call the land
of the free and the home of the brave.

232
00:20:59,843 --> 00:21:02,929
- Scotland !
- No ! America.

233
00:21:02,971 --> 00:21:05,515
[Together]
Oh ! America.

234
00:21:05,598 --> 00:21:10,937
Poppycock. Pushy Americans.
Always showing up late for every war.

235
00:21:11,021 --> 00:21:15,567
Overpaid, oversexed
And over here !

236
00:21:15,650 --> 00:21:17,444
What's eatin' Grandpa ?

237
00:21:17,485 --> 00:21:19,946
Oh, don't mind him,
Mister-- Mister ?

238
00:21:20,030 --> 00:21:23,658
The name's Rocky. Rocky the
Rhode Island Red. Rhodes for short.

239
00:21:23,742 --> 00:21:27,454
- Rocky Rhodes ?
- Catchy, ain't it ?

240
00:21:27,495 --> 00:21:30,415
Um, Mr. Rhodes,
is this you ?

241
00:21:30,498 --> 00:21:34,294
Uh, who wants to know ?

242
00:21:34,336 --> 00:21:36,546
A group of rather
desperate chickens.

243
00:21:36,588 --> 00:21:41,760
You see, if it is you, then you just
might be the answer to our prayers.

244
00:21:41,843 --> 00:21:43,928
[Chuckling]

245
00:21:44,012 --> 00:21:48,641
Well, then, call me a miracle,
doll face, 'cause that's me.

246
00:21:50,101 --> 00:21:52,812
And what brings you
to England, Mr. Rhodes ?

247
00:21:52,896 --> 00:21:56,232
Why, all the beautiful
English chicks, of course.

248
00:21:56,316 --> 00:21:59,402
Give over !

249
00:21:59,486 --> 00:22:01,821
You see, I'm
a traveler by nature.

250
00:22:01,905 --> 00:22:05,992
I did that whole barnyard thing
for a while,
but I couldn't really get into it.

251
00:22:06,076 --> 00:22:09,120
Hi. How are you ? Nope.

252
00:22:09,204 --> 00:22:11,247
The open road.
That's more my style.

253
00:22:11,331 --> 00:22:15,585
Yep, just give me a pack on my back
and point me where the wind blows.

254
00:22:15,669 --> 00:22:18,672
In fact, you know what
they call me back home ?

255
00:22:18,755 --> 00:22:22,676
You're gonna love this.
The Lone Free Ranger.

256
00:22:22,759 --> 00:22:25,637
- Ooh !
- Isn't that great ?

257
00:22:25,679 --> 00:22:28,223
- I knew it was possible.
- Oh, it's possible, all right.

258
00:22:28,306 --> 00:22:30,225
- I knew the answer would come.
- Amen !

259
00:22:30,308 --> 00:22:35,105
We're all going to fly over that fence,
and Mr. Rhodes is going
to show us how, right ?

260
00:22:35,188 --> 00:22:39,526
That's-- What ?
Did you say ''fly'' ?

261
00:22:39,567 --> 00:22:42,487
- You can teach us.
- No, I can't.

262
00:22:42,570 --> 00:22:45,949
- Listen. Shh. You hear that ?
- [Silence]

263
00:22:45,990 --> 00:22:50,620
That's the open road calling my name,
and I was born to answer that call. Bye.

264
00:22:50,704 --> 00:22:54,040
He must have
very good hearing.

265
00:22:54,082 --> 00:22:58,211
Okay, okay, where's the exit ?
Ah, this way.

266
00:22:58,294 --> 00:23:02,507
Mr. Rhodes, um, perhaps I didn't
explain our situation properly.

267
00:23:02,549 --> 00:23:04,926
We lay eggs
day in and day out,

268
00:23:05,010 --> 00:23:07,470
and when we can't lay
any more, they kill us.

269
00:23:07,554 --> 00:23:11,808
It's a cruel world, doll face.
You might as well get used to it.

270
00:23:11,891 --> 00:23:15,228
Which part of ''they kill us''
do you not understand ?

271
00:23:15,311 --> 00:23:17,355
I got my own set
of problems to worry about.

272
00:23:17,397 --> 00:23:19,649
Besides, this birdcage can't
be that hard to bust out of.

273
00:23:19,733 --> 00:23:22,193
In fact, watch me.

274
00:23:22,235 --> 00:23:26,740
It's not so hard to get one
chicken out of here or even two,

275
00:23:26,823 --> 00:23:29,367
but this is about all of us.

276
00:23:29,451 --> 00:23:33,204
- All of you ?
- That's what I've been
trying to tell you.

277
00:23:33,288 --> 00:23:35,206
Wait a minute.
Let me get this straight.

278
00:23:35,290 --> 00:23:38,918
You want to get every chicken in this
place out of here at the same time ?

279
00:23:39,002 --> 00:23:42,380
- Of course.
- You're certifiable.

280
00:23:42,464 --> 00:23:44,924
You can't pull off a stunt
like that. That's suicide.

281
00:23:44,966 --> 00:23:46,468
Where there's a will,
there's a way.

282
00:23:46,551 --> 00:23:50,597
- Couldn't agree more.
I will be leaving that way.
- But--

283
00:23:50,597 --> 00:23:52,140
- Mr. Rhodes ?
- # I'm the type of guy #

284
00:23:52,223 --> 00:23:57,145
- Please!
- # That likes to roam around
I'm never in one-- #

285
00:23:58,229 --> 00:24:00,148
[Gasps]

286
00:24:15,121 --> 00:24:18,583
So that's it.
You're from the circus.

287
00:24:18,625 --> 00:24:20,585
Shh !

288
00:24:20,627 --> 00:24:22,587
You're on the run,
aren't you ?

289
00:24:22,629 --> 00:24:24,673
You wanna keep it down ?

290
00:24:24,756 --> 00:24:27,217
- I'm trying to lay low here.
- [Doorbell Ringing]

291
00:24:27,300 --> 00:24:30,387
I should turn you in
right now.

292
00:24:30,470 --> 00:24:34,265
- You wouldn't. Would you ?
- Give me one reason why I shouldn't.

293
00:24:34,349 --> 00:24:36,476
Because I'm... cute ?

294
00:24:37,894 --> 00:24:40,480
[Squawking]

295
00:24:40,563 --> 00:24:43,400
Hey, hey, hey !
What kind of crazy chick are you ?

296
00:24:43,483 --> 00:24:46,695
- Do you know what'll
happen if he finds me ?
- It's a cruel world.

297
00:24:46,736 --> 00:24:48,697
I just decided.
I don't like you.

298
00:24:48,780 --> 00:24:51,449
I just decided. I don't care.
Now, show us how to fly.

299
00:24:51,533 --> 00:24:54,202
- With this wing ?
- Teach us then.

300
00:24:54,285 --> 00:24:55,662
- No !
- [Squawking]

301
00:24:55,745 --> 00:24:59,374
- [Squawking]
- He's valuable, you say ?

302
00:24:59,457 --> 00:25:01,626
- Sure.
- Get the torch.

303
00:25:01,710 --> 00:25:05,088
Now you listen here, sister.
I'm not going back to that life.

304
00:25:05,130 --> 00:25:07,841
I'm a Lone Free Ranger.
Emphasis on free !

305
00:25:07,924 --> 00:25:10,719
And that's what we want.
Freedom !

306
00:25:10,802 --> 00:25:11,886
[Gasps]

307
00:25:13,513 --> 00:25:16,725
- [Chuckles]
- [Ginger] Fancy that.
They're coming this way.

308
00:25:16,808 --> 00:25:19,144
Oh, oh, no. No. Oh, no.
They're on to me.

309
00:25:19,227 --> 00:25:21,312
Teach us to fly
and we'll hide you.

310
00:25:21,396 --> 00:25:24,149
- And if I don't ?
- [Squawks]

311
00:25:24,190 --> 00:25:26,818
Was your father
by any chance a vulture ?

312
00:25:26,901 --> 00:25:28,820
Do we have a deal ?

313
00:25:34,826 --> 00:25:37,537
[Gate Clatters]

314
00:25:48,465 --> 00:25:50,383
Time to make good
on that deal, doll--

315
00:25:50,467 --> 00:25:53,345
The name is Ginger.

316
00:25:53,428 --> 00:25:55,513
[Groans, Gasps]

317
00:26:10,236 --> 00:26:12,739
- Comfortable ?
- Not really.

318
00:26:12,781 --> 00:26:17,744
- Maybe this will help.
- [Grunts] Nice hideout.

319
00:26:17,827 --> 00:26:20,121
Ouch. I had
more room in my egg.

320
00:26:20,205 --> 00:26:23,750
We've held up our end of the deal.
Tomorrow you hold up yours.

321
00:26:23,833 --> 00:26:25,794
- What deal ?
- The flying !

322
00:26:25,877 --> 00:26:27,921
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Right, right, right. Don't worry.

323
00:26:28,004 --> 00:26:29,964
I'll teach you
everything I know.

324
00:26:30,006 --> 00:26:33,051
Now, which bunk is mine ?

325
00:26:33,134 --> 00:26:35,804
[Shouting]

326
00:26:35,887 --> 00:26:39,265
Absolutely outrageous !

327
00:26:39,349 --> 00:26:42,268
Asking a senior officer
to share his quarters...

328
00:26:42,352 --> 00:26:45,188
and with a non commissioned
Yank, no less.

329
00:26:45,271 --> 00:26:47,649
- Why, back in my day, I'd never--
- Hey !

330
00:26:47,732 --> 00:26:51,152
You weren't exactly
my first choice either.

331
00:26:51,236 --> 00:26:53,613
And scoot over.
Your wing's on my side of the bunk.

332
00:26:53,697 --> 00:26:58,159
Your side of the bunk ?
The whole bunk is my side of the bunk!

333
00:26:58,243 --> 00:27:02,872
Just-- What's that smell ?
Is that your breath ?

334
00:27:02,956 --> 00:27:05,834
It's absolutely
outrageous.

335
00:27:08,962 --> 00:27:09,421
[Chattering]

336
00:27:09,421 --> 00:27:11,548
[Chattering]

337
00:27:11,631 --> 00:27:15,051
[Rocky]
So you wanna fly, huh ?

338
00:27:15,135 --> 00:27:19,014
Well, it ain't gonna be easy, and it
ain't gonna happen overnight either.

339
00:27:19,097 --> 00:27:21,057
You see, flying
takes three things.

340
00:27:21,141 --> 00:27:25,228
Hard work,
perseverance and--

341
00:27:25,311 --> 00:27:28,356
- Hard work.
- You said hard work twice !

342
00:27:28,440 --> 00:27:33,278
That's because it takes
twice as much work as perseverance.

343
00:27:33,361 --> 00:27:36,906
Codswallop !
[Mutters]

344
00:27:38,450 --> 00:27:43,663
Now, the most important thing is
we have to work as a team,

345
00:27:43,747 --> 00:27:46,875
which means... you do
everything I tell you.

346
00:27:49,836 --> 00:27:53,673
Right ! Let's rock and roll.

347
00:28:00,805 --> 00:28:03,933
- Oh. Oh, oh.
- Oh. Oh, oh.

348
00:28:03,975 --> 00:28:06,269
[Grunts]

349
00:28:06,353 --> 00:28:09,397
[Grunting]

350
00:28:15,362 --> 00:28:18,114
[Laughs]

351
00:28:18,198 --> 00:28:20,492
[Grunts]

352
00:28:32,128 --> 00:28:37,008
Mrs. Tweedy !
The chickens are--

353
00:28:37,092 --> 00:28:39,761
Pecking ?

354
00:28:39,803 --> 00:28:44,641
[Rocky] And left, two, three.
And right, two, three.

355
00:28:44,683 --> 00:28:48,812
And... stop right there.
Oh, yeah, down.

356
00:28:48,853 --> 00:28:52,482
Down. Yeah, yeah, make little circles.
That's it. Faster.

357
00:28:52,565 --> 00:28:57,612
Faster.
Oh, yes. Perfect.

358
00:28:57,696 --> 00:29:01,700
Oh, that's the spot.
[Sighs]

359
00:29:01,783 --> 00:29:03,410
[Sighs]

360
00:29:03,451 --> 00:29:05,912
[Clears Throat]

361
00:29:10,792 --> 00:29:13,795
I thought you were going
to teach us how to fly.

362
00:29:13,878 --> 00:29:16,381
That's what I'm doing.

363
00:29:16,464 --> 00:29:19,509
Isn't there usually
some flapping involved ?

364
00:29:19,592 --> 00:29:22,929
Hey, do I tell you
how to lay eggs ?

365
00:29:23,013 --> 00:29:25,473
Relax.
We're making progress.

366
00:29:25,515 --> 00:29:30,854
Really ? I can't help feeling
we're going around in circles.

367
00:29:30,895 --> 00:29:34,941
What the-- Hey ! Cut it out !
You're making me dizzy.

368
00:29:35,025 --> 00:29:37,736
I think they're
ready to fly now.

369
00:29:37,736 --> 00:29:39,779
Good, because they
certainly can't walk anymore.

370
00:29:42,866 --> 00:29:45,618
Up and at 'em, gals.
Let's flap.

371
00:29:48,455 --> 00:29:50,457
[Shouting]

372
00:29:50,540 --> 00:29:54,961
Watch, Fetcher. Let's see if old
Attila the Hen has come to her senses.

373
00:29:55,045 --> 00:29:57,339
[Screaming]

374
00:29:57,380 --> 00:30:01,843
- [Grunts]
- [Screaming]

375
00:30:01,926 --> 00:30:05,805
- It's raining hen !
- [Screaming]

376
00:30:09,100 --> 00:30:11,686
- What's this caper, love ?
- We're flying.

377
00:30:11,770 --> 00:30:13,688
Obviously.

378
00:30:13,772 --> 00:30:18,943
- Flippin 'hell. Look at this, Fetch.
- They're gonna kill themselves.

379
00:30:19,027 --> 00:30:22,572
- Wanna watch ?
- Yeah, all right.

380
00:30:27,410 --> 00:30:30,038
- Ooh !
- Ooh !

381
00:30:30,080 --> 00:30:32,248
- Ahh !
- Ahh !

382
00:30:32,332 --> 00:30:36,920
Hey ! Careful
of those eggs !

383
00:30:37,003 --> 00:30:38,922
[Shrieking]

384
00:30:40,840 --> 00:30:43,718
[Nick]Sunny-side up.
[Laughs]

385
00:30:45,845 --> 00:30:48,223
Now they're over easy !

386
00:30:49,933 --> 00:30:51,851
[Nick]
Definitely scrambled.

387
00:30:53,770 --> 00:30:55,689
Go ! Go ! Go !

388
00:30:55,772 --> 00:30:58,608
Go, go, go, go ! Go !

389
00:30:58,650 --> 00:31:01,236
Poultry in motion !

390
00:31:01,319 --> 00:31:03,405
[Laughing]

391
00:31:12,455 --> 00:31:15,291
[Chattering]

392
00:31:15,375 --> 00:31:17,627
Birds of a feather
flop together.

393
00:31:17,711 --> 00:31:20,171
[Gasping]

394
00:31:23,508 --> 00:31:25,510
Great work, ladies.
Great work !

395
00:31:25,593 --> 00:31:28,972
The pain you're feeling
is a good thing. It's good.

396
00:31:29,055 --> 00:31:31,016
Pain is your friend, okay ?
It's a positive thing.

397
00:31:31,057 --> 00:31:34,602
Just keep the faith there, uh--
What was your name ? Agnes !
You'll get there.

398
00:31:34,686 --> 00:31:36,646
Ducky, I think you
flew four feet today.

399
00:31:36,688 --> 00:31:40,900
Right, four feet !
From the roof to the ground.

400
00:31:40,984 --> 00:31:43,695
It's all part of the process, ladies.
Nothing to worry about.

401
00:31:43,737 --> 00:31:45,739
[Whispers]
Ya cheese-eating little--

402
00:31:45,822 --> 00:31:47,741
- [Rumbling]
- Whoa !

403
00:31:48,825 --> 00:31:51,578
That doesn't sound good.
Ha, ha, ha.

404
00:31:51,661 --> 00:31:54,372
Okay, the ground's shaking.
Are we worried ?

405
00:31:54,414 --> 00:31:56,791
Are we worried ?

406
00:32:03,214 --> 00:32:06,426
The circus.
Quick. Hide me.

407
00:32:06,468 --> 00:32:08,553
- Hide me.
- Come on.

408
00:32:08,636 --> 00:32:13,683
One isn't awarded a medal like this for
flapping about like a lunatic, what.

409
00:32:13,767 --> 00:32:17,020
[Stammers] Now, see here !
This is an officer's quarters.

410
00:32:17,103 --> 00:32:19,522
- Quick. In here.
- Get out of here immediately, sir !

411
00:32:19,564 --> 00:32:21,816
Give it a rest, Pops.

412
00:32:21,900 --> 00:32:25,737
Out of here ! I shall have you
on a charge within the week.

413
00:33:03,983 --> 00:33:06,069
Cheers, mate.

414
00:33:06,152 --> 00:33:09,114
[Truck Departing]

415
00:33:09,197 --> 00:33:11,116
## [Whistling]

416
00:33:11,199 --> 00:33:15,245
It's all in your head.
It's all in your head.

417
00:33:15,328 --> 00:33:17,372
It's all in your head.

418
00:33:20,917 --> 00:33:23,628
Ooh !

419
00:33:23,712 --> 00:33:27,215
What-- What--
What's all this then ?

420
00:33:27,298 --> 00:33:29,592
This is our future,
Mr. Tweedy.

421
00:33:29,676 --> 00:33:33,972
No more wasting time with petty
egg collection and minuscule profits.

422
00:33:34,014 --> 00:33:38,018
No more eggs ?
But we've always been egg farmers.

423
00:33:38,101 --> 00:33:41,271
Me father and his father and all
their fathers. They was always--

424
00:33:41,354 --> 00:33:45,150
Poor ! Worthless.
Nothings.

425
00:33:45,233 --> 00:33:47,152
But all that's about to change.

426
00:33:47,235 --> 00:33:50,655
This will take Tweedy's farm
out of the dark ages...

427
00:33:50,697 --> 00:33:54,451
and into full-scale
automated production.

428
00:33:54,534 --> 00:33:59,414
- [Gasps]
- Melisha Tweedy will be poor no longer.

429
00:33:59,497 --> 00:34:02,208
Ooh !

430
00:34:02,292 --> 00:34:05,378
I'll put it together
then, shall I ?

431
00:34:11,259 --> 00:34:13,261
This isn't good, Mac.

432
00:34:13,345 --> 00:34:17,432
Whatever's in those boxes is for us,
and I don't think it's softer hay.

433
00:34:17,515 --> 00:34:20,018
Aye, hen. And I hate
to be the voice of doom,

434
00:34:20,101 --> 00:34:24,522
but I've been calculating my figures,
and I just don't think
we're built for flyin'.

435
00:34:24,606 --> 00:34:28,234
But I saw him.
He flew in over that fence.

436
00:34:28,318 --> 00:34:30,236
Aye, aye, I believe you,

437
00:34:30,320 --> 00:34:34,741
but if we could
just see it for ourselves,
that may answer some questions.

438
00:34:34,824 --> 00:34:37,035
You're right. I'm sorry.

439
00:34:37,118 --> 00:34:39,579
We've been at this all week,
and we're getting nowhere.

440
00:34:39,621 --> 00:34:45,001
If his wing were better, he could--
Oh ! I'll have a word with him.

441
00:34:50,965 --> 00:34:52,676
Where is he ?

442
00:34:52,759 --> 00:34:56,680
They didn't give me this medal
for being a Yank nanny.

443
00:34:56,721 --> 00:34:59,099
A simple ''I don't know''
would suffice.

444
00:34:59,140 --> 00:35:02,977
Beware of that one,
young Ginger.

445
00:35:03,061 --> 00:35:05,522
That Yank is not
to be trusted.

446
00:35:05,605 --> 00:35:09,901
That Yank is our ticket
out of here.

447
00:35:09,984 --> 00:35:13,947
And the pig says to the horse,
''Hey, fella, why the long face ?''

448
00:35:15,865 --> 00:35:18,868
Oh, oh, look, look.

449
00:35:18,952 --> 00:35:22,247
Oh. Cocktail !

450
00:35:22,288 --> 00:35:23,873
Give over !

451
00:35:25,083 --> 00:35:26,876
[Gasps]

452
00:35:28,086 --> 00:35:33,008
So, um, anyway--

453
00:35:33,091 --> 00:35:37,053
Remember those flying tips tomorrow.
They're very important.

454
00:35:37,137 --> 00:35:40,015
Keep thinking
those flighty thoughts.

455
00:35:40,098 --> 00:35:42,392
Oh, yeah.

456
00:35:42,434 --> 00:35:44,394
They're swell chicks.
They really are.

457
00:35:44,436 --> 00:35:49,357
Look at what Babs made me.
A beakwarmer. Isn't that the cutest ?

458
00:35:49,441 --> 00:35:53,278
And that bunty. [Laughs]
She really packs a punch.

459
00:35:53,278 --> 00:35:55,739
Is there a problem here ?

460
00:35:55,822 --> 00:35:57,907
- Have we flown over that fence ?
- Not quite.

461
00:35:57,991 --> 00:36:01,286
- Then there's a problem.
- Good things come to those
who wait, doll face.

462
00:36:01,369 --> 00:36:03,329
Ginger !

463
00:36:11,963 --> 00:36:14,549
- Okay, how long did it take you ?
- To do what ?

464
00:36:14,632 --> 00:36:16,593
To learn how to fly.

465
00:36:16,634 --> 00:36:19,554
Apples and oranges, baby doll.
I'm gifted. They're not.

466
00:36:19,637 --> 00:36:22,223
You can't compare
the two, okay ?

467
00:36:22,307 --> 00:36:24,434
The point is,
these things take time.

468
00:36:24,517 --> 00:36:26,478
Which we are rapidly
running out of.

469
00:36:26,519 --> 00:36:28,605
- We haven't even lifted
off the ground. Why ?
- Thrust.

470
00:36:28,688 --> 00:36:33,276
I went over my calculations,
and I figured the key element
we're missing is thrust.

471
00:36:36,571 --> 00:36:38,573
I-I didn't get
a word of that.

472
00:36:38,656 --> 00:36:43,119
Thrust ! Other birds like ducks
and geese, when they take off,
what do they have ? Thrust.

473
00:36:43,203 --> 00:36:45,997
I swear she ain't
usin' real words.

474
00:36:46,081 --> 00:36:49,042
- She said we need more thrust.
- Oh, thrust.

475
00:36:49,125 --> 00:36:54,381
Well, of course, we need thrust.
Thrust and flying are like this.
That's flying and that's thrust.

476
00:36:54,464 --> 00:36:58,301
- Would you excuse us ?
- Aye.

477
00:36:58,385 --> 00:37:00,720
Ah, the wing,
the wing, the wing.

478
00:37:00,804 --> 00:37:03,473
If we don't see some results
by tomorrow, the deal is off,
and you're on your own.

479
00:37:03,515 --> 00:37:08,228
No more hiding.
The farmers will find you,
and it's back to the circus, flyboy.

480
00:37:08,311 --> 00:37:13,566
You're the first chick I ever met
with the shell still on.

481
00:37:13,650 --> 00:37:18,571
Sleep tight, angel face. The Rock's
on the case. [Clicks Tongue]

482
00:37:18,613 --> 00:37:21,700
Ginger!

483
00:37:21,783 --> 00:37:23,702
Whew !

484
00:37:25,370 --> 00:37:30,834
[Fowler clears Throat]
Cock-a-doodle-doo! What, what.

485
00:37:32,168 --> 00:37:35,505
- [Nick]Oh, it was a beaut, guv'nor.
- Hmm ?

486
00:37:35,588 --> 00:37:39,009
A fine piece of work,
If I do says so meself.

487
00:37:39,092 --> 00:37:41,011
- I say so meself too.
- I wish I could have seen it.

488
00:37:41,094 --> 00:37:44,556
We slipped into the farmer's room,
all quiet like.

489
00:37:44,639 --> 00:37:47,726
- Like a fish.
- Yeah, and we--

490
00:37:47,809 --> 00:37:52,188
'' Like a fish'' ?
You stupid Norbert.

491
00:37:52,272 --> 00:37:54,399
Anyway, guv, here it is.

492
00:37:54,482 --> 00:37:57,360
- El merchandiso.
- That's Spanish.

493
00:37:57,444 --> 00:38:01,406
- What are these two crooks doing here ?
- So, you know each other.

494
00:38:01,489 --> 00:38:03,783
She don't think
we're valuable.

495
00:38:03,867 --> 00:38:06,536
Guys, you are
without a doubt the sneakiest,

496
00:38:06,619 --> 00:38:09,247
most light-fingered
thieving parasites I've ever met.

497
00:38:09,330 --> 00:38:13,501
- Oh, don't, don't. Stop it.
- I've gone bright red.

498
00:38:13,585 --> 00:38:15,503
So, uh, how about them eggs ?

499
00:38:15,587 --> 00:38:18,381
- Eggs ? Don't tell me
you promised them--
- Yep !

500
00:38:18,423 --> 00:38:20,425
Promised them every egg
I lay this month.

501
00:38:20,508 --> 00:38:23,762
And when can we expect
the first installment ?

502
00:38:23,845 --> 00:38:27,182
I'm brewing one up as we speak, guys.
I'll keep you posted.

503
00:38:28,767 --> 00:38:31,311
Pleasure doing business
with you, sir.

504
00:38:31,394 --> 00:38:33,313
Sucker.

505
00:38:35,273 --> 00:38:37,400
- What ?
- You've lied to them.

506
00:38:37,484 --> 00:38:41,613
I didn't lie, doll face.
I just... omitted certain truths.

507
00:38:41,696 --> 00:38:43,615
I'll give them exactly
what I promised.

508
00:38:43,698 --> 00:38:46,284
- Which is nothing.
- Which is what I'll give them.

509
00:38:46,368 --> 00:38:49,496
And what
will you give us ?

510
00:38:49,579 --> 00:38:51,247
Thrust !

511
00:38:53,667 --> 00:38:56,294
[Rocky]
You okay, sweetheart ?Good, good.

512
00:38:58,713 --> 00:39:00,590
Now this is just
a little helper.

513
00:39:00,632 --> 00:39:02,592
Something to get you going.
It's a thrust exercise.

514
00:39:02,634 --> 00:39:06,388
- The tension's killing me.
- It's gonna kill her !

515
00:39:06,429 --> 00:39:09,099
- Release !
- Whoa !

516
00:39:11,101 --> 00:39:13,311
[Whimpers]

517
00:39:13,353 --> 00:39:15,522
Come on ! Flap !

518
00:39:18,733 --> 00:39:21,820
You can do it.
Flap, flap, flap !

519
00:39:25,615 --> 00:39:28,660
Yes, yes, yes !

520
00:39:30,412 --> 00:39:33,623
Is that your first offense ?

521
00:39:33,707 --> 00:39:36,292
- [Screaming]
- [Screaming]

522
00:39:40,463 --> 00:39:44,009
[Crashing]

523
00:39:44,092 --> 00:39:47,637
- Oops. [Chuckles]
- [Bell Ringing]

524
00:39:48,930 --> 00:39:52,892
Roll call !
I haven't laid any eggs.

525
00:39:52,976 --> 00:39:55,186
- Hide me.
- Three days and no tone.

526
00:39:55,270 --> 00:39:58,023
- Oh, no !
- Why didn't you tell us, Babs ?
- Hide me !

527
00:39:58,106 --> 00:39:59,691
We've been so busy
with the flying--

528
00:39:59,774 --> 00:40:01,526
- They're coming !
- Hide me !

529
00:40:01,568 --> 00:40:04,279
Hide yourself!

530
00:40:04,320 --> 00:40:09,034
[Shouting, Chattering]

531
00:40:11,953 --> 00:40:13,955
Oh !

532
00:40:24,341 --> 00:40:27,594
[Whimpering]

533
00:40:59,209 --> 00:41:01,670
[Chuckles]

534
00:41:05,507 --> 00:41:07,467
Double their food rations,
Mr. Tweedy.

535
00:41:07,550 --> 00:41:10,845
I want them all
as fat as this one.

536
00:41:11,971 --> 00:41:13,932
Oh !

537
00:41:15,475 --> 00:41:19,646
All of me life flashed
before me eyes !

538
00:41:19,729 --> 00:41:21,773
It was really borin'.

539
00:41:23,733 --> 00:41:27,946
Chicken feed.
My favorite !

540
00:41:28,029 --> 00:41:29,781
Wait. Wait.

541
00:41:29,864 --> 00:41:33,368
[Chattering]

542
00:41:33,451 --> 00:41:35,370
Ooh !

543
00:41:36,454 --> 00:41:38,164
No. Wait !

544
00:41:41,501 --> 00:41:45,630
Babs, please ! Bunty !
Stop it ! Wait !

545
00:41:45,714 --> 00:41:47,632
Stop !

546
00:41:52,554 --> 00:41:55,181
Stop it !

547
00:41:56,391 --> 00:42:01,312
Something is wrong here.
Can't you see that ?

548
00:42:01,354 --> 00:42:03,314
Strange boxes
arrive in the barn.

549
549:47:31,084 --> 550:29:34,398
00:42:02,995 --> 00:42:05,020
Babs stops laying, but they
don't take her to the chop,

550
00:42:05,483 --> 00:42:07,861
and now they're giving us
extra food.

551
00:42:07,902 --> 00:42:11,322
Don't you see what's happening ?
They're fattening us up.

552
00:42:11,406 --> 00:42:15,243
- They're going to kill us all.
- [Gulping]

553
00:42:15,326 --> 00:42:19,330
Whoa, whoa ! Heavy alert.
[Laughs]

554
00:42:19,414 --> 00:42:21,833
- She didn't mean that, gals.
- Do you mind ?

555
00:42:21,875 --> 00:42:24,085
Keep eating.
Save some for me.

556
00:42:24,169 --> 00:42:27,464
What are you doing ?
How dare you ! Let go of me !

557
00:42:27,464 --> 00:42:32,761
Listen. I've met some
hard-boiled eggs in my day,

558
00:42:27,464 --> 00:42:32,761
558
00:42:32,458 --> 00:42:35,518
- What's that supposed to mean ?
- It means you got to lighten up.

559
00:42:35,972 --> 00:42:37,974
Over in America,
we have this rule.

560
00:42:38,016 --> 00:42:40,852
If you want to motivate someone,
don't mention death.

561
00:42:40,935 --> 00:42:44,773
Funny. Over here, the rule is:
Always tell the truth.

562
00:42:44,814 --> 00:42:47,567
That's been working like
a real charm, hasn't it ?

563
00:42:47,609 --> 00:42:51,279
Here's some free advice.
You want them to perform ?
Tell them what they wanna hear.

564
00:42:51,363 --> 00:42:53,823
You mean lie.

565
00:42:53,865 --> 00:42:57,494
Here we go again.
You know what your problem is ?

566
566:48:33,805 --> 567:31:31,299
00:42:57,182 --> 00:42:59,207
You're... difficult.

567
00:42:59,704 --> 00:43:03,875
Why ? Because I'm honest ?
I care about what happens to them,

568
00:43:03,958 --> 00:43:07,337
something I wouldn't expect a lone
free ranger to know anything about.

569
00:43:07,420 --> 00:43:10,131
If this is the way you show it,
I hope you never care about me.

570
00:43:10,173 --> 00:43:13,510
- I can assure you, I never will.
- Good !
- Fine !

571
00:43:15,845 --> 00:43:17,639
[Gasps]

572
00:43:51,131 --> 00:43:53,174
[Radio Static]

573
00:43:53,258 --> 00:43:56,386
# [Woman Vocalizing,
Accordion]

574
00:43:56,469 --> 00:43:59,222
[Static]

575
00:43:59,264 --> 00:44:02,142
-# [Orchestra]
- [Chattering]

576
00:44:02,225 --> 00:44:04,144
What's all this ?

577
00:44:04,227 --> 00:44:08,440
Well, here she is.
Ask and you shall receive.

578
00:44:08,481 --> 00:44:12,318
- That's biblical.
- That's real craftsmanship
is what it is.

579
00:44:12,360 --> 00:44:15,113
- Solid as a rock.
- Ooh !

580
00:44:15,196 --> 00:44:18,074
- [Static]
- It's supposed to do that.

581
00:44:18,158 --> 00:44:22,495
- It's perfect, guys.
- And how's that egg coming ?

582
00:44:22,579 --> 00:44:25,915
This is a double yolker.

583
00:44:25,999 --> 00:44:29,836
- [Chuckling]
- [Voices, Static]

584
00:44:29,919 --> 00:44:32,005
# [Jazz On Radio,
Static]

585
00:44:32,047 --> 00:44:34,049
[Voices, Static]

586
00:44:34,090 --> 00:44:36,384

- # [Jazz]
- I don't see what this has to do with--

587
00:44:36,468 --> 00:44:38,845
You will.

588
00:44:38,887 --> 00:44:40,972
We've been workin' too hard.

589
00:44:41,056 --> 00:44:43,725
Time to kick back a bit,
shake those tail feathers.

590
00:44:43,767 --> 00:44:47,437
Look at him.
Nelly podging around like a--

591
00:44:47,520 --> 00:44:49,898
Oh, good heavens.
What's happenin' ?

592
00:44:49,981 --> 00:44:54,402
That's called a beat, sister.
Feel it pulsing through your body ?

593
00:44:54,486 --> 00:44:58,031
Oh, yes. Pulsing.
Fancy that.

594
00:44:58,114 --> 00:45:01,159
Hey, well,
then go with it, baby.

595
00:45:01,242 --> 00:45:05,830
Oh, my. Look !
I'm going with it !

596
00:45:05,914 --> 00:45:08,667
Bunty, what's got into you ?

597
00:45:08,750 --> 00:45:10,877
Same thing that's got
into you apparently.

598
00:45:10,919 --> 00:45:13,421
[Man On Radio]
# Flip, flop, fly #

599
00:45:13,505 --> 00:45:15,799
-# I don't care if I die #
-Just go with the flow, gal !

600
00:45:15,882 --> 00:45:18,343
-# Flip, flop, fly #
- Let it go !

601
00:45:18,385 --> 00:45:20,887
# I don't care if I die #

602
00:45:20,970 --> 00:45:24,140
# Don't ever leave me
Don't ever say good-bye #

603
00:45:24,224 --> 00:45:27,352
Now, see here. I don't
recall authorizing a hop.

604
00:45:27,435 --> 00:45:29,437
Oh, shut up and dance.

605
00:45:29,521 --> 00:45:32,941
- Oh ! Oh !
- [Laughing]

606
00:45:35,276 --> 00:45:40,198
-[Crying]
-What are you sobbing about, you nancy ?

607
00:45:40,281 --> 00:45:46,162
Little moments like this, mate.
It's what makes the job all worthwhile.

608
00:45:49,457 --> 00:45:51,418
Wanna dance ?

609
00:45:53,545 --> 00:45:55,463
Yeah, all right.

610
00:45:55,547 --> 00:45:59,134
#Now, give me one more kiss
Hold it along, long time#

611
00:45:59,217 --> 00:46:00,802
Huh ?

612
00:46:00,885 --> 00:46:06,141
# Give me one more kiss
Hold it along, long time #

613
00:46:06,224 --> 00:46:08,518
# Love me, baby, till the feelin'
hits my head like wine #

614
00:46:08,601 --> 00:46:10,645
# So fine
So glad you're mine #

615
00:46:10,729 --> 00:46:13,023
# Flip, flop, fly #

616
00:46:13,064 --> 00:46:15,817
# I don't care if I die #

617
00:46:15,900 --> 00:46:20,113
# Flip, flop, fly
I don't care if I die #

618
00:46:20,196 --> 00:46:24,951
# Don't ever leave me
Don't ever say good-bye#

619
00:46:25,035 --> 00:46:28,705
# Don't ever leave me
Don't ever say good-bye # 

620
00:46:28,788 --> 00:46:32,959
# Yeah, don't ever leave me
Don't ever say good-bye #

621
00:46:33,043 --> 00:46:35,879
-# Yeah #
- [Screaming]
- Ooh !

622
00:46:35,962 --> 00:46:38,715
##[Ends]

623
00:46:38,798 --> 00:46:43,470
[Giggles]
Did ya see that ? I flew !

624
00:46:43,553 --> 00:46:46,056
Atta girl, Babsy.
Atta girl.

625
00:46:46,139 --> 00:46:49,642
- Oh ! Your wing. It's better.
- Well--

626
00:46:49,726 --> 00:46:52,687
- How about that ?
- Fantastic.

627
00:46:52,729 --> 00:46:54,898
You can fly for us
tomorrow.

628
00:46:54,981 --> 00:46:58,485
Uh, uh, yeah, so it seems.

629
00:46:58,568 --> 00:47:00,362
I flew ! I flew !

630
00:47:00,403 --> 00:47:04,157
Looks like I owe you
an apology.

631
00:47:04,240 --> 00:47:07,619
I didn't think you cared about us,
but after all this--

632
00:47:07,702 --> 00:47:10,163
Well, it seems I was wrong.

633
00:47:10,246 --> 00:47:13,291
Hey, easy, Miss Hard-boiled.

634
00:47:13,375 --> 00:47:15,627
I might think
you're turning soft.

635
00:47:15,710 --> 00:47:17,921
# [Slow Jazz On Radio]

636
00:47:20,256 --> 00:47:24,636
Uh, listen, there's
something I got to tell ya.

637
00:47:24,719 --> 00:47:26,930
- I--
- [Rumbling, Electricity Crackles]

638
00:47:27,013 --> 00:47:30,016
[Group Exclaiming]

639
00:47:30,100 --> 00:47:35,271
- [Chattering]
- No. You'd better wait here.

640
00:47:36,773 --> 00:47:40,944
[Dogs Barking]

641
00:47:41,027 --> 00:47:43,071
[Rumbling]

642
00:47:48,993 --> 00:47:52,414
[Machinery Chugging]

643
00:47:54,082 --> 00:47:56,209
[Beeping]

644
00:47:58,628 --> 00:48:02,882
Ooh, that's champion,
that is. What is it ?

645
00:48:02,966 --> 00:48:05,885
It's a pie machine,
you idiot.

646
00:48:05,969 --> 00:48:08,596
Chickens go in,
pies come out.

647
00:48:08,680 --> 00:48:10,640
Ooh !
What kind of pies ?

648
00:48:10,682 --> 00:48:13,393
- Apple.
- My favorite !

649
00:48:13,476 --> 00:48:18,690
Chicken pies, you great lummox !
Imagine it.

650
00:48:18,773 --> 00:48:21,818
In less than a fortnight,
every grocers' in the county...

651
00:48:21,901 --> 00:48:24,404
will be stocked
with box upon box...

652
00:48:24,446 --> 00:48:27,991
of Mrs. Tweedy's
Homemade Chicken Pies.

653
00:48:28,074 --> 00:48:29,617
Just Missus ?

654
00:48:29,701 --> 00:48:32,787
Woman's touch. Makes the public
feel more comfortable.

655
00:48:32,871 --> 00:48:36,291
Oh, right.
How does it work ?

656
656:55:06,865 --> 657:43:43,156
00:48:35,921 --> 00:48:38,856
- [Gasps]
- Get me a chicken and I'll show you.

657
00:48:40,503 --> 00:48:43,131
I know just the one.

658
00:48:43,214 --> 00:48:46,259
- [Growling]
- [Gasps]

659
00:48:46,343 --> 00:48:50,347
I've got a score
to settle with you.

660
00:48:50,430 --> 00:48:52,557
Bloomin' heck !
They've got Ginger !

661
00:48:57,479 --> 00:49:00,607
We mustn't panic.
We mustn't panic !

662
00:49:01,941 --> 00:49:03,902
- [All Screaming]
- [Fowler]Quiet there !

663
00:49:03,943 --> 00:49:08,073
Quiet, I say !
Let's have some discipline, what, what.

664
00:49:08,156 --> 00:49:11,868
The enemy has taken a prisoner.
This calls for retaliation!

665
00:49:11,951 --> 00:49:15,372
- Retaliation !
- What's going on ? What's happening ?

666
00:49:15,413 --> 00:49:19,376
They got Ginger, Mr. Rhodes.
They're taking her to the chop !

667
00:49:19,459 --> 00:49:23,838
Well, what are you waiting for, laddie ?
Fly over there. Save her !

668
00:49:23,880 --> 00:49:28,051
Of course-- No, no !
No, that's just what they'd expect.

669
00:49:28,134 --> 00:49:30,470
But I say we give them
the old element of surprise.

670
00:49:30,553 --> 00:49:33,515
And catch Jerry
with his trousers down.

671
00:49:33,556 --> 00:49:36,059
I like the sound of that.
What's the plan ?

672
00:49:36,142 --> 00:49:38,520
The plan-- The plan.

673
00:49:38,561 --> 00:49:40,563
The plan-- Uh, Babs !

674
00:49:40,647 --> 00:49:43,566
Give me that thing.
Bunty, give me a boost.

675
00:49:45,485 --> 00:49:49,197
[Shouting]

676
00:49:49,280 --> 00:49:51,449
[Grunts]

677
00:49:51,533 --> 00:49:55,412
[Machinery Chugging,
Whirring]

678
00:49:55,495 --> 00:49:57,414
Whoa.

679
00:49:57,497 --> 00:50:00,041
Look at the size
of that thing.

680
00:50:00,125 --> 00:50:02,961
[Grunting]

681
00:50:03,837 --> 00:50:05,505
Oh, no !

682
00:50:06,798 --> 00:50:09,259
Chickens go in,

683
00:50:09,300 --> 00:50:11,386
pies come out.

684
00:50:14,639 --> 00:50:16,516
[Chuckles]
Chicken pies.

685
00:50:16,599 --> 00:50:18,476
Not--
Not apple pies.

686
00:50:18,560 --> 00:50:20,061
[Mr. Tweedy]
Chicken!

687
00:50:25,859 --> 00:50:27,402
[Ginger Gasps]

688
00:50:27,485 --> 00:50:29,654
Oh, great.
Brilliant !

689
00:50:29,738 --> 00:50:32,157
- Yo, baby doll !
- Rocky !

690
00:50:32,240 --> 00:50:33,950
- I'm coming !
- Hurry !

691
00:50:35,076 --> 00:50:37,662
- I'm still coming !
- Come on !

692
00:50:37,746 --> 00:50:41,332
- Stop this thing !
- I'm gettin' there !

693
00:50:43,626 --> 00:50:45,545
Oh, shoot !

694
00:50:45,587 --> 00:50:47,964
[Ginger]
Rocky !

695
00:50:48,006 --> 00:50:50,342
I'll be down before you can say...
[Gasps]

696
00:50:51,009 --> 00:50:52,552
mixed vegetables !

697
00:50:52,635 --> 00:50:55,305
Aaaah !

698
00:50:55,388 --> 00:50:57,349
[Gasps]

699
00:50:57,390 --> 00:50:59,768
Aaah ! Ohh !

700
00:50:59,851 --> 00:51:02,270
[Yelling Continues]

701
00:51:02,312 --> 00:51:05,648
Whoa-ohh-ohh-ohh !

702
00:51:12,113 --> 00:51:14,074
Whoa-ohh-ohh !

703
00:51:14,157 --> 00:51:15,909
D-oh !
Get it ?

704
00:51:15,992 --> 00:51:18,370
- Dough !
- I'm stuck !

705
00:51:18,453 --> 00:51:20,372
Nothing to it.
Oops.

706
00:51:21,456 --> 00:51:23,416
[Grunting]

707
00:51:29,881 --> 00:51:31,591
Ohh ! Oh !

708
00:51:36,680 --> 00:51:38,390
Hang on !

709
00:51:42,936 --> 00:51:44,229
Look out !

710
00:51:46,940 --> 00:51:49,109
[Both Gasp]

711
00:51:49,192 --> 00:51:51,111
[Both]
Whoa !

712
00:51:59,828 --> 00:52:02,497
Hey ! Aha !

713
00:52:07,961 --> 00:52:09,879
- Yes !
- [Laughing]

714
00:52:15,468 --> 00:52:17,303
[Gasping, Panting]

715
00:52:17,345 --> 00:52:19,305
Oh, it's like
an oven in here.

716
00:52:19,347 --> 00:52:21,766
- [Hissing]
- [Gasping]

717
00:52:28,481 --> 00:52:30,150
Come on !

718
00:52:30,233 --> 00:52:32,485
Wait up !
I'm com--

719
00:52:33,653 --> 00:52:35,113
Don't leave-

720
00:52:35,780 --> 00:52:37,991
Get over to the--

721
00:52:39,242 --> 00:52:41,244
[Rocky
Shouting Unintelligibly]

722
00:52:48,293 --> 00:52:50,712
The door ! Come on !
[Grunts]

723
00:52:54,299 --> 00:52:56,509
[Both Screaming]

724
00:53:14,152 --> 00:53:16,321
She's gonna blow !
Run !

725
00:53:17,405 --> 00:53:18,990
[Alarm Bell Ringing]

726
00:53:19,074 --> 00:53:21,868
- Huh ?
- [Bell Continues Ringing]

727
00:53:21,910 --> 00:53:24,371
What did you do,
you great pudding ?

728
00:53:24,454 --> 00:53:26,373
I didn't do 'owt !

729
00:53:34,881 --> 00:53:37,717
- Turn it off !
- It won't turn off !

730
00:53:43,390 --> 00:53:46,017
[Both Yelling]

731
00:53:43,390 --> 00:53:46,017

732
00:54:01,579 --> 00:54:04,810
- Ouch !
- We've got to show the others. Come on.

732
00:54:05,412 --> 00:54:07,330
[Sighs]

733
00:54:07,414 --> 00:54:09,541
[Muttering]

734
00:54:09,624 --> 00:54:12,419
[Machinery Shutting Down]

735
00:54:14,045 --> 00:54:16,381
Look ! I fixed it !

736
00:54:16,423 --> 00:54:18,174
Huh ?

737
00:54:18,258 --> 00:54:20,844
[Chickens Gasping,
Exclaiming]

738
00:54:20,927 --> 00:54:23,930
- Chicken pies ?
- Ohh !
- Oh, no !

739
00:54:24,014 --> 00:54:26,933
- Yes, but--
- I don't want to be a pie.

740
00:54:27,017 --> 00:54:30,228
- [Chickens Continue Exclaiming]
- I don't like gravy.

741
00:54:30,311 --> 00:54:33,523
Ladies, please.
Let's not lose our heads.

742
00:54:33,606 --> 00:54:35,567
Lose our heads ?

743
00:54:43,575 --> 00:54:47,495
What I meant to say was, Rocky sabotaged
the machine and bought us more time.

744
746:02:11,022 --> 746:56:58,517
00:54:47,058 --> 00:54:48,992
- Ooh !
- Ooh !

745
00:54:49,581 --> 00:54:52,459
And better still,
he's going to fly for us tomorrow.

746
00:54:52,500 --> 00:54:55,920
- [Cheering]
- And once we've seen how's it done,
we'll get it.

747
00:54:56,004 --> 00:54:57,922
So don't worry,

748
00:54:58,006 --> 00:55:01,968
because tomorrow everything's going
to go much, much smoother.

749
00:55:09,476 --> 00:55:11,102
[Grunts]

750
00:55:11,186 --> 00:55:13,772
All right, Pops,
what did I do now ?

751
00:55:13,855 --> 00:55:16,274
A very brave
and honorable deed, sir.

752
00:55:18,401 --> 00:55:21,988
[Clears Throat] In the light
of your action this evening, I--

753
00:55:22,072 --> 00:55:25,867
I dutifully admit that
I have misjudged your character.

754
00:55:27,494 --> 00:55:31,706
So I present you with this
medal for bravery. [Chuckles]

755
00:55:31,748 --> 00:55:33,708
And...

756
00:55:33,750 --> 00:55:36,169
I salute you.

757
00:55:38,421 --> 00:55:40,131
In honor
of the occasion,

758
00:55:40,173 --> 00:55:43,385
I surrender the bunk
entirely.

759
00:55:43,426 --> 00:55:46,554
I shall sleep under the stars.
[Chuckles]

760
00:55:48,556 --> 00:55:52,560
Oh, uh, I await tomorrow's
flying demonstration...

761
00:55:52,644 --> 00:55:55,230
with great anticipation.

762
00:55:57,899 --> 00:56:00,360
You and me both, Pops.

763
00:56:09,285 --> 00:56:11,371
- Oh !
- I'm sorry. Were you--

764
00:56:11,454 --> 00:56:13,873
- Is this your-- I'll get down.
- No, no, it's just--

765
00:56:13,957 --> 00:56:16,042
- Since you're here--
- No, I'm glad you're here, because--

766
00:56:16,126 --> 00:56:18,044
- I'm sorry. You go first.
- You go ahead. I'll--

767
00:56:18,128 --> 00:56:20,005
[Chuckles]

768
00:56:20,046 --> 00:56:22,590
Um, I just wanted
to say...

769
00:56:22,674 --> 00:56:25,593
I may have been
a bit harsh at first.

770
00:56:25,677 --> 00:56:29,055
Well,
what I really mean is,

771
00:56:29,097 --> 00:56:31,057
thank you...

772
00:56:31,099 --> 00:56:33,560
for saving my life.

773
00:56:33,643 --> 00:56:36,396
For saving our lives.

774
00:56:36,479 --> 00:56:38,565
You know,

775
00:56:38,606 --> 00:56:40,567
I come up here
every night...

776
00:56:40,608 --> 00:56:44,738
and look out to that hill
and just imagine what it must
be like on the other side.

777
00:56:44,821 --> 00:56:47,282
It's funny, I've--

778
00:56:47,365 --> 00:56:50,827
I've never actually felt
grass beneath my feet.

779
00:56:50,910 --> 00:56:52,829
I'm sorry.

780
00:56:52,912 --> 00:56:56,249
Here I am rambling on about hills
and grass, and you had something to say.

781
00:56:56,291 --> 00:56:58,251
Uh, y-y-yeah.

782
00:56:58,293 --> 00:57:02,380
Um, it's just that,
y-you know,

783
00:57:02,464 --> 00:57:06,676
life as I've experienced it,
you know, out there,

784
00:57:06,760 --> 00:57:09,095
lone free rangin' and stuff,
it's, uh,

785
00:57:09,179 --> 00:57:12,223
it's full of disappointments
and, uh--

786
00:57:12,307 --> 00:57:15,143
What, you mean grass isn't
all it's cracked up to be ?

787
00:57:15,185 --> 00:57:17,145
Grass !
Exactly. Grass.

788
00:57:17,187 --> 00:57:20,148
It's always greener
on the other side.

789
00:57:20,190 --> 00:57:24,778
And then you get there
and it's brown and prickly.

790
00:57:24,861 --> 00:57:26,905
You see
what I'm tryin' to say ?

791
00:57:30,116 --> 00:57:33,078
What I'm trying to say is,

792
00:57:35,455 --> 00:57:38,917
[Sighs]
you're welcome.

793
00:57:38,958 --> 00:57:40,919
You know,

794
00:57:40,960 --> 00:57:45,924
that hill is looking closer tonight
than it ever has before.

795
00:57:47,509 --> 00:57:49,636
Oh !

796
00:57:49,719 --> 00:57:53,932
[Clears Throat]
Well, good night... Rocky.

797
00:57:55,517 --> 00:57:57,977
Good night... Ginger.

798
00:58:00,939 --> 00:58:03,191
[Sighs]

799
00:58:20,041 --> 00:58:21,960
[Chickens Chattering]

800
00:58:22,043 --> 00:58:25,714
Company, attention !

801
00:58:25,797 --> 00:58:27,799
[Chattering
Continues]

802
00:58:30,719 --> 00:58:33,471
Well, today's the day, girls.
We're going to fly !

803
805:06:33,601 --> 806:05:07,072
00:58:33,017 --> 00:58:35,747
- I can feel it !
- [Cheering, Laughing]

804
00:58:36,349 --> 00:58:39,686
Finally, we get to see
a real professional in action.

805
00:58:39,769 --> 00:58:42,689
Better start warming up.
I'll go and get him.

806
00:58:42,772 --> 00:58:45,150
- Rocky. Knock-knock.
- [Knock On Door]

807
00:58:45,233 --> 00:58:48,153
Everyone's waiting,
so I told them to--

808
00:58:52,907 --> 00:58:54,868
R-Rocky ?

809
00:59:49,214 --> 00:59:50,965
[Thunder crashing]

810
01:00:38,221 --> 01:00:40,765
[Mac]
Oh, a cannon.

811
01:00:40,807 --> 01:00:42,851
Aye, that would
give you thrust.

812
01:00:42,934 --> 01:00:44,978
I knew he was fake
all along.

813
01:00:45,061 --> 01:00:49,149
In fact, I'm not even certain
he was American.

814
01:00:49,232 --> 01:00:51,985
So, what's
the next plan, hen ?

815
01:00:52,068 --> 01:00:53,987
[Sighs]
Let's face it.

816
01:00:54,070 --> 01:00:56,990
The only way out of here
is wrapped in pastry.

817
01:00:57,073 --> 01:00:58,658
[Chickens Gasping]

818
01:00:58,742 --> 01:01:00,994
Perhaps he just
went on holiday.

819
01:01:01,077 --> 01:01:04,330
Perhaps he just went to get away
from your infernal knitting !

820
01:01:04,372 --> 01:01:07,334
- [Chickens Gasping, Exclaiming]
- Ohh ! Ohh !

821
01:01:07,375 --> 01:01:10,712
You were the one that was always
hitting him. See how you like it.

822
01:01:10,795 --> 01:01:13,631
Don't push me, four-eyes !

823
01:01:13,715 --> 01:01:16,801
- [All Yelling, Chattering]
- Quiet there !

824
01:01:16,885 --> 01:01:18,845
Quiet, I say !

825
01:01:18,887 --> 01:01:22,557
Dissension in the ranks.
Precisely what Jerry would have wanted.

826
01:01:22,640 --> 01:01:24,309
The old
divide and conquer.

827
01:01:24,392 --> 01:01:28,563
A proper squadron work together,
like we did in my R.A.F. days.

828
01:01:28,646 --> 01:01:31,566
Jocko at the stick,
Flappy at the map...

829
01:01:31,649 --> 01:01:34,069
and old Whizzbang
at the tail-end Charlie.

830
01:01:34,152 --> 01:01:37,405
WingCo would give the call,
hop in the old crate, chocks away !

831
01:01:37,489 --> 01:01:40,742
Wizard show it was.
That's how you get medals.

832
01:01:40,784 --> 01:01:44,913
Will you shut up about
your stupid blooming medals !

833
01:01:44,996 --> 01:01:47,248
- Ooh !
- [Chickens Gasp]

834
01:01:49,167 --> 01:01:51,920
Ohh !

835
01:01:52,003 --> 01:01:54,089
How dare you !

836
01:01:54,172 --> 01:01:56,508
- [Groans]
- Madam, forgive me.

837
01:01:56,591 --> 01:01:58,635
A-As an officer,
I offer my most--

838
01:01:58,718 --> 01:02:01,179
- [Chickens Gasping, Shouting]
- [Groans]

839
01:02:15,110 --> 01:02:17,028
Fowler ?

840
01:02:18,196 --> 01:02:20,115
[Shouting Continues]

841
01:02:20,198 --> 01:02:22,659
Everyone, shut up !

842
01:02:22,701 --> 01:02:24,035
[Shouting Quiets]

843
01:02:24,119 --> 01:02:25,829
Eh ?

844
01:02:31,543 --> 01:02:33,920
[Clears Throat]
Fowler.

845
01:02:34,004 --> 01:02:36,256
What exactly is
the R.A.F. ?

846
01:02:36,339 --> 01:02:38,758
What do you mean,
what is it ?

847
01:02:38,842 --> 01:02:41,386
The Royal Air Force is what.
[Chuckles]

848
01:02:41,469 --> 01:02:44,848
Then what's
the ''old crate'' ?

849
01:02:46,641 --> 01:02:49,269
Ahh !
There she is.

850
01:02:51,354 --> 01:02:53,231
Gorgeous,
isn't she ?

851
01:02:53,273 --> 01:02:56,234
You mean, you flew
in one of these ?

852
01:02:56,276 --> 01:02:59,738
Beautifully built. In fact, there's
a bit of a story to that as well.

853
01:02:59,821 --> 01:03:01,740
We were out on a ''recce,''
you see.

854
01:03:01,823 --> 01:03:04,743
Ops had given the go-ahead,
but the weather duffed up.

855
01:03:04,826 --> 01:03:07,704
- Yes. Of course.
- [Fowler continues]

856
01:03:07,746 --> 01:03:10,707
We might actually be able
to pull this off.

857
01:03:10,790 --> 01:03:14,127
- We're still going to fly out of here.
- What, what ?

858
01:03:14,169 --> 01:03:16,046
Fowler's
provided the answer.

859
01:03:16,129 --> 01:03:18,048
I have ?

860
01:03:18,131 --> 01:03:21,009
Uh, yes, yes, yes.
Of course I have.

861
01:03:21,092 --> 01:03:23,011
Uh, how have I ?

862
01:03:23,094 --> 01:03:25,055
We'll make...

863
01:03:25,096 --> 01:03:27,057
a crate.

864
01:03:27,098 --> 01:03:29,851
[Ginger]
Mac, you'll handle the engineering.

865
01:03:30,935 --> 01:03:32,687
Babs, manufacturing.

866
01:03:32,771 --> 01:03:34,981
Fowler will be
Chief aviation advisor.

867
01:03:35,065 --> 01:03:36,691
Bunty, eggs.

868
01:03:36,775 --> 01:03:38,360
- Eggs ?
- Eggs.

869
01:03:38,443 --> 01:03:41,571

Right, just like the ones
that rooster was gonna lay.

870
01:03:41,654 --> 01:03:44,574
Only roosters don't lay eggs,
do they ?

871
01:03:44,657 --> 01:03:47,577
- Don't they ?
- No, it's a lady thing, apparently.

872
01:03:47,660 --> 01:03:49,579
Ask your mum.

873
01:03:49,662 --> 01:03:52,999
One egg for every item on the list.
First payment in advance.

874
01:03:53,083 --> 01:03:55,210
[Simultaneously]
Right ! When do we start ?

875
01:03:55,293 --> 01:03:57,212
- [Slurps]
- Come on !

876
01:03:58,296 --> 01:04:00,256
- [Giggles]
- Hey.

877
01:04:00,298 --> 01:04:02,759
- Oh !
- # [Humming]

878
01:04:05,970 --> 01:04:08,640
Huh ?

879
01:04:08,682 --> 01:04:10,642
What the dickens ?

880
01:04:12,143 --> 01:04:15,105
Oh, gnomes now.

881
01:04:19,734 --> 01:04:22,195
- Voila !
- [Giggles]

882
01:04:22,237 --> 01:04:25,198
- Give me.
- [All Chattering]

883
01:04:35,875 --> 01:04:37,002
Hmm ?

884
01:04:38,503 --> 01:04:40,255
Aah !

885
01:04:53,810 --> 01:04:57,355
- Ohh ! [Giggles]
- All right, here.

886
01:04:59,941 --> 01:05:02,610
[Squealing]

887
01:05:04,738 --> 01:05:06,656
[Grunting]

888
01:05:06,698 --> 01:05:08,867
Eggs from heaven !

889
01:05:08,950 --> 01:05:12,120
- No ! From her bum !
- [Laughs]

890
01:05:15,915 --> 01:05:20,045
[All Grunting]

891
01:05:25,008 --> 01:05:26,426
[Chickens Cheering]

892
01:05:28,094 --> 01:05:31,139
[Machinery Chugging]

893
01:05:33,892 --> 01:05:36,311
[Continues Chugging]

894
01:05:36,394 --> 01:05:39,397
[Siren Blaring,
Machinery Shuts Down]

895
01:05:39,481 --> 01:05:41,399
Mmm ?

896
01:05:43,276 --> 01:05:46,696
- Idiot !
- That was close.

897
01:05:46,738 --> 01:05:48,782
Too close.

898
01:05:48,865 --> 01:05:51,701
We can't stop now.
Come on, everyone ! Go for it !

899
01:05:51,785 --> 01:05:54,829
Really go for it !
Go, go, go, go !

900
01:05:57,207 --> 01:05:59,626
- Mac, we need
those calculations quickly.
- Uh-huh.

901
01:05:59,709 --> 01:06:02,420
Agnes, that has to be
really secure.

902
01:06:02,504 --> 01:06:04,881
- Careful up there, Fowler !
- Roger!

903
01:06:05,965 --> 01:06:07,884
Bunty,
give him a hand.

904
01:06:07,967 --> 01:06:09,761
Well done, Babs.
Keep it up.

905
01:06:09,844 --> 01:06:12,180
No problem, doll face.

906
01:06:19,979 --> 01:06:22,941
# [Rhythm And Blues]

907
01:06:27,362 --> 01:06:30,323
[Singing Along With Radio]
# Oh, I'm the type of guy #

908
01:06:30,407 --> 01:06:32,367
# That likes
to roam around #

909
01:06:32,450 --> 01:06:34,411
# I'm never in one place #

910
01:06:34,494 --> 01:06:37,205
# I roam from town to town #

911
01:06:37,247 --> 01:06:40,792
# And when I found myself
fallin' for some girl #

912
01:06:40,875 --> 01:06:42,836
# I'd hop
right in that car-- #

913
01:06:42,877 --> 01:06:44,838
[Radio Continues]
# And travel 'round the world #

914
01:06:44,879 --> 01:06:47,173
# 'Cause I'm a wanderer #

915
01:06:47,257 --> 01:06:49,134
# Yeah
A wanderer #

916
01:06:49,217 --> 01:06:51,636
# I roam around and 'round
Around and 'round #

917
01:06:51,720 --> 01:06:53,638
# [Continues]

918
01:06:53,722 --> 01:06:55,140
# 'Cause
I'm a wanderer #

919
01:06:55,223 --> 01:06:56,766
# Yeah, a wanderer #

920
01:06:56,850 --> 01:06:58,309
Oh, boy.

921
01:06:58,351 --> 01:07:00,729
# I roam around and 'round
Around and 'round, around #

922
01:07:01,771 --> 01:07:04,399
[Motor Cranking]

923
01:07:04,482 --> 01:07:06,276
Come on.

924
01:07:06,359 --> 01:07:08,611
[Groans]

925
01:07:08,695 --> 01:07:10,613
Please.

926
01:07:10,697 --> 01:07:13,908
[Motor Starts,
Machinery Chugging]

927
01:07:13,992 --> 01:07:17,412
Oh, no.
He's fixed it.

928
01:07:19,956 --> 01:07:21,875
[Laughs]

929
01:07:21,958 --> 01:07:25,587
- [Thunder crashing]
- Get the chickens.

930
01:07:25,670 --> 01:07:27,297
Which ones ?

931
01:07:28,381 --> 01:07:30,008
All of them.

932
01:07:37,015 --> 01:07:39,768
Me tools !

933
01:07:39,809 --> 01:07:42,604
Why, you thieving
little buggers !

934
01:07:42,645 --> 01:07:45,106
What's the plan ?

935
01:07:48,610 --> 01:07:50,362
- Attack !
- Huh ?

936
01:07:50,445 --> 01:07:52,238
- [Grunting]
- [Groaning]

937
01:07:52,322 --> 01:07:53,615
Nice plan.

938
01:07:55,200 --> 01:07:57,494
- [Chickens Shouting]
- Mrs. Tweedy !

939
01:07:59,954 --> 01:08:03,041
Aaaah! 
Mrs. Tweedy !

940
01:08:03,124 --> 01:08:05,585
The chickens
are revolting !

941
01:08:05,627 --> 01:08:07,921
Finally,
something we agree on.

942
01:08:08,963 --> 01:08:10,757
Help ! Mrs.--

943
01:08:10,840 --> 01:08:12,634
[Whining]

944
01:08:13,802 --> 01:08:15,679
Mmm-- Mmm ?

945
01:08:15,762 --> 01:08:17,430
Under the hut.

946
01:08:17,472 --> 01:08:21,351
- Come on !
- [Chickens Continue
Shouting, Chattering]

947
01:08:25,313 --> 01:08:28,066
- What have we done ?
- This is it, everyone.

948
01:08:28,149 --> 01:08:30,110
We're escaping.

949
01:08:30,151 --> 01:08:32,487
- What, now ?
- Now !

950
01:08:32,570 --> 01:08:35,657
- But, Ginger, she's not ready.
- Listen.

951
01:08:35,740 --> 01:08:38,868
We'll either die free chickens
or die trying.

952
01:08:38,952 --> 01:08:41,079
[All Cheering]

953
01:08:41,162 --> 01:08:43,373
Are those
the only choices ?

954
01:08:43,456 --> 01:08:45,917
- Let's do it.
- Scramble !

955
01:08:52,674 --> 01:08:54,426
[Squawks]

956
01:08:59,305 --> 01:09:01,224
This way !

957
01:09:09,441 --> 01:09:11,901
- [Gasps]
- [All Grunting]

958
01:09:32,297 --> 01:09:34,632
[Chuckling]

959
01:09:34,716 --> 01:09:37,635
[Muffled Shout]
Mrs. Tweedy !

960
01:09:38,845 --> 01:09:41,765
The exits are located
here and here.

961
01:09:41,848 --> 01:09:44,809
In the quite likely event
of an emergency,

962
01:09:44,851 --> 01:09:46,811
put your head
between your knees and--

963
01:09:46,853 --> 01:09:48,938
Kiss your bum good-bye.

964
01:09:48,980 --> 01:09:51,149
All right, Fowler,
ready for takeoff.

965
01:09:51,232 --> 01:09:53,985
Behind you
all the way.

966
01:09:55,487 --> 01:09:57,906
But you're
supposed to be up there.

967
01:09:57,989 --> 01:09:59,657
You're the pilot.

968
01:09:59,699 --> 01:10:03,995
- Oh, don't be ridiculous.
I can't fly this contraption.
- [Chickens Gasping]

969
01:10:04,079 --> 01:10:07,165
Back in your day--
the Royal Air Force--

970
01:10:07,248 --> 01:10:10,126
6-4-4 Squadron,
poultry division.

971
01:10:10,168 --> 01:10:12,128
We were the mascots.

972
01:10:12,170 --> 01:10:14,756
You mean you never
actually flew the plane ?

973
01:10:14,839 --> 01:10:16,758
Good heavens, no.

974
01:10:16,841 --> 01:10:19,302
- I'm a chicken.
- [All Gasp]

975
01:10:19,386 --> 01:10:24,474
The Royal Air Force doesn't
let chickens behind the controls
of a complex aircraft.

976
01:10:24,557 --> 01:10:27,018
- We're all gonna die !
- [Screaming, Wailing]

977
01:10:27,060 --> 01:10:29,020
Fowler,
you have to fly it.

978
01:10:29,062 --> 01:10:32,315
You're always talking about back
in your day. Well, today is your day.

979
01:10:34,818 --> 01:10:37,946
You can do it,
You old sausage.

980
01:10:39,781 --> 01:10:41,950
Wing Commander
T.I. Fowler...

981
01:10:42,033 --> 01:10:43,952
reporting for duty.

982
01:10:44,035 --> 01:10:46,496
[Chickens Cheering]

983
01:10:46,579 --> 01:10:49,499
Well, come on.
What are you waiting for ?

984
01:10:49,582 --> 01:10:53,420
We haven't got all day.
Let's get this crate off the ground.

985
01:10:53,461 --> 01:10:54,879
[Ginger]
Fowler! Now!

986
01:10:54,963 --> 01:10:57,340
Roger ! Contact !

987
01:10:57,424 --> 01:10:59,342
[All Grunting]

988
01:11:09,310 --> 01:11:11,229
Cleared for takeoff !

989
01:11:18,028 --> 01:11:19,863
Chocks away !

990
01:11:19,946 --> 01:11:22,073
[Simultaneously]
Chocks away !

991
01:11:22,157 --> 01:11:24,242
Whoa !

992
01:11:29,539 --> 01:11:33,418
- Full throttle !
- Full throttle !

993
01:11:54,481 --> 01:11:56,900
We need more power !

994
01:11:56,983 --> 01:12:01,279
I cannot work miracles, Cap'n !
We're givin' her all she's got !

995
01:12:10,330 --> 01:12:13,667
- Gotcha !
- Hard right !

996
01:12:15,502 --> 01:12:17,045
Oh, mother !

997
01:12:18,129 --> 01:12:19,839
[Groans]

998
01:12:22,342 --> 01:12:25,011
Turn her around.
I'll get the ramp.

999
01:12:25,095 --> 01:12:26,846
[Grunts, Panting]

1000
01:12:33,895 --> 01:12:36,606
Aaah !

1001
01:12:38,650 --> 01:12:41,277
- Put the ramp down.
- [Gasps]

1002
01:12:44,447 --> 01:12:46,616
You are going to be
a pie !

1003
01:12:46,700 --> 01:12:48,868
[Bicycle Bell Jingles]

1004
01:12:50,453 --> 01:12:54,666
Ginger !

1005
01:12:54,749 --> 01:12:57,961
Rocky !

1006
01:13:04,759 --> 01:13:06,386
Heads up !

1007
01:13:10,306 --> 01:13:12,350
[Gasps]

1008
01:13:13,977 --> 01:13:15,478
[Sighs]

1009
01:13:16,730 --> 01:13:19,149
[Sighs]

1010
01:13:19,232 --> 01:13:21,693
- [Bell Jingles]
- Look out!

1011
01:13:21,693 --> 01:13:24,279
- Aah !
- Clear the runway !

1012
01:13:36,124 --> 01:13:38,168
[Gasps]

1013
01:13:44,424 --> 01:13:47,052
Ginger! Let's go!

1014
01:13:51,097 --> 01:13:53,350
- We're flying !
- [Excited Chattering]

1015
01:14:05,820 --> 01:14:08,573
- Aah !
- That's for leaving.

1016
01:14:08,615 --> 01:14:10,033
Eew.

1017
01:14:10,116 --> 01:14:13,161
And this
is for coming back.

1018
01:14:14,871 --> 01:14:16,831
- Whoa !
- Uhh !

1019
01:14:16,873 --> 01:14:20,001
- [All Screaming, Clucking]
- Great Scot ! What was that ?

1020
01:14:20,085 --> 01:14:24,589
A cling-on, Cap'n !
And the engines can't take it !

1021
01:14:24,673 --> 01:14:26,800
- [Snarls]
- [Both Scream]

1022
01:14:28,343 --> 01:14:30,095
Oh, goodness.

1023
01:14:30,136 --> 01:14:31,554
Babs ! Scissors !

1024
01:14:33,807 --> 01:14:35,225
Bingo.

1025
01:14:35,308 --> 01:14:36,935
Lower me down.

1026
01:14:37,018 --> 01:14:38,645
- But, Ginger, I--
- Just do it.

1027
01:14:38,728 --> 01:14:41,106
[Fowler]
Increase velocity !

1028
01:14:41,189 --> 01:14:44,943
- What does that mean ?
- It means pedal
your flippin' giblets out !

1029
01:14:57,831 --> 01:15:00,166
- Lower !
- I'm trying !

1030
01:15:04,421 --> 01:15:06,673
- Aah !
- Aaah !

1031
01:15:06,756 --> 01:15:09,175
- Fowler, look out!
- [Gasps]

1032
01:15:17,058 --> 01:15:19,894
- Whoa !
- Oh ! Ginger !

1033
01:15:22,981 --> 01:15:25,525
[Snarls]

1034
01:15:29,279 --> 01:15:31,114
Fire ! Fire !

1035
01:15:33,658 --> 01:15:36,161
- Me eggs.
- [Blubbering]

1036
01:15:37,787 --> 01:15:40,331
No !
[Gasps]

1037
01:15:40,415 --> 01:15:44,836
Blea-aah !
[Growls]

1038
01:15:44,878 --> 01:15:46,713
More ammo !
Hurry !

1039
01:15:46,796 --> 01:15:49,007
- We got no more eggs !
- Ginger !

1040
01:15:49,090 --> 01:15:51,718
Look out!

1041
01:15:51,801 --> 01:15:55,263
[Snarling]

1042
01:15:59,017 --> 01:16:02,520
No !

1043
01:16:09,277 --> 01:16:12,405
[Groans]

1044
01:16:14,199 --> 01:16:16,743
- Huh ?
- Bye-bye.

1045
01:16:16,826 --> 01:16:19,954
- Aaah !
- Bombs away !

1046
01:16:20,038 --> 01:16:22,874
- Mr. Tweedy !
- [All Cheering]

1047
01:16:22,957 --> 01:16:25,460
Oh, that was good.
That was good !

1048
01:16:27,837 --> 01:16:30,298
The old bird bought it !
[Laughing]

1049
01:16:31,466 --> 01:16:34,052
Mrs. Tweedy !
Mrs. Twee--

1050
01:16:34,094 --> 01:16:37,389
[Shrieking]

1051
01:16:37,472 --> 01:16:40,475
- [Siren Blaring, Alarm Bell Ringing]
- [Gasping]

1052
01:16:42,143 --> 01:16:45,355
[Alarm Continues,
Bell Continues]

1053
01:16:52,070 --> 01:16:54,030
- [Explosion]
- Whoa !

1054
01:17:06,251 --> 01:17:09,963
I told you
they was organized.

1055
01:17:11,131 --> 01:17:14,134
[Snarling]

1056
01:17:20,432 --> 01:17:22,392
We did it, everyone !

1057
01:17:22,434 --> 01:17:24,811
[All Cheering]

1058
01:17:32,485 --> 01:17:35,155
- [Giggling, Laughing]
- [Sobbing]

1059
01:17:35,238 --> 01:17:36,823
Ha, ha, ha, ha--

1060
01:17:42,120 --> 01:17:43,538
[All]
Aww !
 
1062
01:17:42,899 --> 01:17:45,197
- [All Exclaiming]
- Whoa!

1061
01:17:45,999 --> 01:17:48,960
[Fowler]
Keep peddling ! We 're not there yet!

1062
01:17:52,714 --> 01:17:56,301
You can't see paradise
if you don't pedal!

1063
01:17:58,720 --> 01:17:59,054
Put your drumsticks
into it!

1064
01:17:59,054 --> 01:18:01,306
Put your drumsticks
into it!

1065
01:18:01,389 --> 01:18:03,850
[Imitating
Airplane Engine]

1066
01:18:05,143 --> 01:18:07,604
That's what I told him,
what, what.

1067
01:18:07,687 --> 01:18:11,399
We were losing altitude, you see,
and heading for a fearful prang.

1068
01:18:11,483 --> 01:18:13,902
This is a lovely holiday.

1069
01:18:13,985 --> 01:18:15,904
I'll be sad to go back.

1070
01:18:15,987 --> 01:18:18,907
Safety at all times
is imperative.

1071
01:18:18,948 --> 01:18:20,909
Now,
wind 'er up and...

1072
01:18:20,950 --> 01:18:22,911
- Whee !
- let 'er go !

1073
01:18:22,952 --> 01:18:24,996
- [Excited Chattering]
- So...

1074
01:18:25,080 --> 01:18:26,998
is it as good
as you imagined ?

1075
01:18:27,082 --> 01:18:29,209
- No.
- [Gasps]

1076
01:18:29,292 --> 01:18:32,462
- It's better.
- [Chuckles]

1077
01:18:32,545 --> 01:18:35,965
- Come on. I'll show you
how to play cricket.
- [Chattering Continues]

1078
01:18:39,803 --> 01:18:42,055
[Nick]
'Ey, 'ey, here 's a thought.

1079
01:18:42,097 --> 01:18:45,350
Why don't we get an egg
And start our own chicken farm ?

1080
01:18:45,433 --> 01:18:48,353
That way we'll have
all the eggs we could eat.

1081
01:18:48,436 --> 01:18:50,897
Right.
We'll need a chicken then.

1082
01:18:50,980 --> 01:18:52,816
No.
No, we'll need an egg.

1083
01:18:52,899 --> 01:18:56,319
You have the egg first.
That's where you get the chicken from.

1084
01:18:56,361 --> 01:18:59,322
No, that's cobblers. If you don't have
a chicken, where you gonna get an egg ?

1085
01:18:59,406 --> 01:19:02,325
From the chicken
that comes from the egg.

1086
01:19:02,409 --> 01:19:05,328
Yeah, but you have to have
an egg to have a chicken.

1087
01:19:05,412 --> 01:19:08,331
Yeah, but you gotta get
the chicken first to get the egg,

1088
01:19:08,415 --> 01:19:11,334
and then the egg--
you get the chicken out.

1089
01:19:11,418 --> 01:19:13,837
Hang on.
Let's go over this again.

1090
01:19:20,927 --> 01:19:22,846
Yeow!

1091
01:19:22,929 --> 01:19:25,682
All right.

1092
01:19:25,765 --> 01:19:27,892
Yeah.

